<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pécs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sopianae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pécs is a city of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baranya">Baranya</a> county, at the foot of the Mecsek hills. Founded as the Roman town of Sopianae, it has an early Christian necropolis now on the World Heritage list. In 1367 the first university in Hungary was founded there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pecs.jpg" alt="Pécs" width="320" height="332" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Imoti95 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P%C3%A9cs_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
